# UX workflow: verify bottom-left reset depth guardrails.
# Purpose: Step focus and step selection expose the same shallow/deep model:
# tap resets step values while preserving child content; hold performs the deep
# reset that removes child content.
# Expect: capture_changed:step_3_enabled=step_3_reset_by_tap, capture_changed:step_3_reenabled=selection_deep_reset_applied_by_hold

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen pattern_focus

# Move directly from Pattern to Step focus.
150 tap NAV 60
350 capture screen step_focus

# Enable a visible step, then reset only that focused step with a tap.
750 tap MACRO_3 60
950 capture screen step_3_enabled
1050 tap BOTTOM_LEFT 60
1250 capture screen step_3_reset_by_tap

# Enable the same step again, enter root Step selection with LEFT_TOP, and
# select it. Long NAV is reserved for Structure.
1350 tap MACRO_3 60
1550 capture screen step_3_reenabled
1650 tap LEFT_TOP 60
1900 capture screen step_selection_entered
3000 tap MACRO_3 60
3200 capture screen step_3_selected

# A short press applies the shallow selected-step reset and keeps selection
# active so the user can see what changed.
3300 tap BOTTOM_LEFT 60
3500 capture screen selection_tap_shallow_reset

# Long press arms and applies the deep selected-step reset.
3600 button BOTTOM_LEFT down
3800 capture screen selection_reset_hold_started
4700 tick
4750 capture screen selection_deep_reset_applied_by_hold
4800 button BOTTOM_LEFT up
5050 capture screen selection_reset_released
